      "side": 1,
      "message": "When mode \u003d\u003d CHARGE_CONTROL_IDLE, the charge current is set to 0. So, the system will run on the AC power and the battery will naturally drain.\n\nThe current implementation supports one gear for charging (NORMAL) and two gears: slow (IDLE) and fast (DISCHARGE) for discharging. Slow discharge is used while the SoC is in the target range.",
